A hospital rule says at least one doctor must stay on call per shift. Two on-call doctors press "Go off call" at the same moment. Each request runs in PostgreSQL at REPEATABLE READ:

```sql
BEGIN;
SELECT count(*) FROM doctors WHERE shift_id = 7 AND on_call;  -- returns 2
UPDATE doctors SET on_call = false WHERE id = $me AND shift_id = 7;
COMMIT;
```

Both commit and nobody is on call. Which two changes prevent this? (Choose two.)
